## Summary

Removes the deprecated local `withTemporaryFiles()` helper and replaces all usages with `usingTemporaryFiles()` from the `using-temporary-files` devDependency. Pure test refactoring — no production code changes.

**Before:**
```js
await withTemporaryFiles(
  { "routes/pet.ts": "export const GET = () => ({ status: 200 });" },
  async (tempDir, { path: getPath }) => {
    await pruneRoutes(tempDir, ["/pet"]);
    await fs.access(getPath("routes/pet.ts"));
  },
);
```

**After:**
```js
await usingTemporaryFiles(async ($) => {
  await $.add("routes/pet.ts", "export const GET = () => ({ status: 200 });");
  await pruneRoutes($.path(""), ["/pet"]);
  await fs.access($.path("routes/pet.ts"));
});
```

**Note on Windows compatibility:** `usingTemporaryFiles` returns native OS paths, whereas the old `withTemporaryFiles` helper always normalized paths to forward slashes. The `Transpiler` class requires forward-slash paths for its internal string replacement logic, so a small `forwardSlash()` helper was added in `transpiler.test.ts` to normalize paths before passing them to the `Transpiler` constructor.

